.PP
\fBArguments and options\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<MUTATION\-ID>\fR
Mark one failed Mutation skipped before running sync.

Skipping a failed close relinquishes it rather than bypassing it: the Item returns to open and loses its Closing Reason, Dependencies it resolved as their Blocking Item become unresolved, and an accepted Ticket becomes selectable by `tk next` again.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.PP
Sync first pulls Backend changes for tracked open Items, then applies queued
Mutations in order. Unresolved title/body edits protect those fields from
Pull; other Shared Fields can still refresh. Sync requires a configured Remote.
.PP
A failed Mutation stops later Mutations from applying. Inspect it with
.B tk sync log
and retry sync after fixing the cause. Use
.B \-\-skip
to give up a failed non-Promotion Mutation; the skip commits before Backend
access. An indeterminate Promotion is not replayed automatically: use
.BR "tk promote reconcile" ,
.BR "tk promote retry" ,
or
.BR "tk promote cancel" .
